From 7e9646f0b9d0ee68f7bc051389bb50d9220cce69 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dominggoes Isakh <drjisakh@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 13:43:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 17/18] WindowManager: Hold the boot animation until the boot
 has settled

On slow hardware BOOT_COMPLETED starts so much work that the phone stays at
full CPU load for about a minute after the home screen appears, and apps can
hit ANRs in that time.

Tell ActivityManager the animation is complete while it is still showing, so
boot finishes behind it. End the animation once CPU use has stayed below 50%
for three 2 s samples, or after 180 s. Keep the screen on in the meantime,
because the screen timeout starts when boot completes.

The home screen now appears after about 117 s instead of about 61 s, with the
CPU already mostly idle.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
